    {
      "block_id": "2605.06070_p9_b34",
      "text": "In this paper, we propose ArenaPO, an efficient preference optimization framework for diffusion\nmodels that extracts fine-grained preference from Arena without relying on an explicit reward\nmodel. By modeling each source model\u2019s capability as a Gaussian distribution, and interpreting\nbinary annotations as observations induced by uncertainty, ArenaPO can estimate quality gaps\nbetween image pairs using latent-variable inference via truncated normal distribution. These fine-\ngrained preferences are then seamlessly integrated into training, combining the efficiency of offline\noptimization with richer preference signals. Extensive experiments on Pick-a-Pic v2 and HPD v3\ndemonstrate consistent and significant improvements over existing DPO-based methods, validating\nthe effectiveness and practicality of ArenaPO for diffusion model alignment.\n",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        625.1,
        505.65,
        722.41
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        432,
        2500,
        2022,
        2889
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 846,
      "block_type": 0
    },
